The offline compiler publishes every block it compiles (FEX 3bec2ac, on top of 0019)

The window program's code map had 91 blocks of ucrtbase. The offline
compiler compiled all of them, but its cache held only 74. The other 17
were exactly the blocks it logged as "[fexlock] UNPUB-COMPILE". In
CompileBlock, a nonzero emission-lock depth or CodeBufferWriteMutex
stamp in the TEB is read as a guest exception delivered under the
compiler's own locks (ml455). Such a block is compiled for one run
and never entered into the lookup cache, so the cache written from it
lacks the block. Every run then compiles the block at run time, and
converge-cache.sh finds the ready code maps already hold it.

The offline compiler delivers no guest exceptions and compiles on one
thread, so while a cache is being generated CompileBlock now compiles
and publishes as usual, with "[aot-gen] X: emission locks look held
while generating a cache; compiled and published as usual" (first 8).

